  "verbalization": "Doxorubicin is implicated in the interaction with EW-12 through multiple distinct biological pathways, each involving different molecular targets. The evidence suggests that doxorubicin may act as a target for several unrelated receptors or proteins, including G-protein coupled receptor 132, P2X purinoceptor 1, and LC4-1. These targets are all involved in signaling pathways that ultimately lead to the activation of EW-12. While the exact mechanism by which these targets influence EW-12 remains unclear, the shared role of these pathways in cellular signaling implies a potential convergent or indirect relationship between doxorubicin and EW-12. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of drug-target interactions, where a single molecule can influence multiple biological processes through diverse molecular mechanisms.",
